# Keep the knowledge graph scoped to the system being built.
#
# ⚠️⚠️ THE LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING AND WAS MISSING UNTIL 2026-09-20.
# `archive/` with no slash matches a directory named `archive` AT ANY DEPTH, so when
# `docs/plan/archive/` was created on 2026-09-19 it was silently swallowed by the rule
# written for `archive/power-platform/` — and ~9,200 lines of CLOSED BUT TRUE plan
# history disappeared from `graphify query`, which is the first navigation tool every
# session is told to use. Nothing went red: an ignore rule that over-matches produces
# a smaller graph, not an error. `/archive/` is anchored to the repository root.
#
# The Power Platform era is kept for its reasoning (see archive/power-platform/README.md)
# but it is ~3.9MB of superseded documentation. Indexing it means every
# `graphify query` competes against decisions that are no longer true — including
# four ADRs that ADR-035 §1 proves were never true.
/archive/

# ⚠️ `docs/plan/archive/` IS DELIBERATELY NOT IGNORED, and the difference matters.
# `/archive/` describes a system NOBODY IS BUILDING. `docs/plan/archive/` is this
# system's own closed history — every line of it was true when written, and for
# several owner rulings about what a screen renders IT IS THE ONLY RECORD THAT
# EXISTS (§2.11 keeps rendering out of scope, so there is no constraint, grant or
# policy to hold them). A query result carries its `source_file`, so an answer from
# `docs/plan/archive/` is self-labelling as closed work — check the path before
# citing it as current.

